Implementation plan (phases)

Phase 0 — Discovery & design (1 day)
- Inspect existing bulk-RADIUS spec (specs/001-radius-wlan-config) and reuse data model and command-line UX decisions.
- Identify existing helper functions for listing WLANS, rate limiting, CSV export, env loading.

Phase 1 — Core scan & preview (2 days)
- Implement scanning routine that calls listOrgWlans and filters RADIUS WLANS.
- Implement preview display: indices, site, wlan name/id, current timer values.
- Load and display .env defaults at startup.
- Add robust selection parser for "all", indices, ranges, and combinations (reuse parsing utilities in src/input if present).

Phase 2 — Apply changes & templates (2 days)
- Implement update logic for site-level WLAN updates using the Mist API updateSiteWlan or appropriate endpoint.
- Implement template update flow: detect WLANs with template_id, prompt user with explicit choices (skip / update template) and implement template update path if chosen.
- Ensure skipping WLANs already matching target values.

Phase 3 — Audit CSV, logging, and retries (1 day)
- Add CSV export of before/after states and per-WLAN status (success/failure), write to data/ with timestamped filename.
- Integrate existing retry/rate-limit utilities; ensure partial failures handled and logged.

Phase 4 — Tests, docs, release (1 day)
- Add unit tests for selection parsing and for the function that computes diffs (current->proposed).
- Add manual test instructions in specs folder and quickstart note for interactive and automated runs (--yes).
- Update README or menus registration to include function_ref WLANRadiusTimerManager.manage.

Milestones and verification
- M1: Successful scan and preview for a sample test org (manual verification). (end Phase 1)
- M2: Successful apply with CSV produced for test org; template updates optional validated. (end Phase 2/3)
- M3: Automated tests and documentation added. (end Phase 4)

Rollout considerations
- Default behavior is interactive requiring APPLY confirmation; provide --yes CLI flag for automation but still write audit CSV.
- Add cautionary help text about editing templates and potential cascading changes.
